ped it.\n- **Hotel: Midtown Lodge (reservation R0003):** New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, $378 total. This was the cheapest hotel under $250/night.\n\nThe total is under $1000, so this trip didn't need manager approval.\n\n**What went wrong along the way:** My first booking request timed out. When I retried it, the system said the flight had been booked and charged ($289, R0001) but the hotel booking had failed. I cancelled that flight booking and refunded it, then sent the full request again, and it went through. I checked Dana's reservations afterward. The only confirmed bookings are R0002 and R0003, and R0001 shows as cancelled, so nothing was double-booked or double-charged.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013TgBDUgE8H4xLt6VPF9vRt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"origin": "SFO", "destination": "JFK", "date": "2026-11-12"}, "name": "search_flights", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TBnZF2hJctGWSZYM2y7p1J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"city": "New York", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2}, "name": "search_hotels", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Total: $289 + $378 = $667, under $1000.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01HaxwDeVHJEmpXnzKkq6ryM", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id": "F100", "hotel_id": "H1", "traveler": "Dana Lee", "checkin": "2026-11-12", "nights": 2, "idempotency_key": "dana-lee-trip-F100-H1-20261112"}, "name": "book_trip", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Retrying with the same idempotency key is safe. It won't book anything twice; it just reports what happened the first time.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GmU8oRLwtUk8DkSzUGhDZ2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"flight_id